e to sessionStorage with automatic clearing.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Add schema validation (e.g., Zod, io-ts) to parseConfig() to ensure config structure matches expected RuntimeConfig.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Remove infrastructure details from user-facing error messages. Log full errors server-side; return generic messages to frontend.\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Sanitize API responses before rendering (use textContent instead of innerHTML, or DOMPurify for HTML content).\",\n    \"MEDIUM: Implement SRI (Subresource Integrity) for npm dependencies in vite.config.ts.\",\n    \"LOW: Add 401 handler that clears token AND redirects to login page with notification.\",\n    \"LOW: Enhance contentEditable check to use getSelection().focusNode and walk parent chain.\",\n    \"BEST PRACTICE: Implement rate limiting for API requests on frontend to detect abuse patterns.\",\n    \"BEST PRACTICE: Add request/response logging and monitoring to detect suspicious patterns.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Key Findings Summary\n\n**Critical Issues** (3):\n1. **JWT in localStorage** - Any XSS vulnerability gives attackers permanent token access\n2. **HTTP by default** - MITM attacks possible on all API communication in production\n3. **Weak URL validation** - Could allow redirect or protocol confusion exploits\n\n**Medium Issues** (5):\n- Unencrypted cache storage, missing CSRF tokens, information disclosure in errors, unvalidated config deserialization, unsanitized responses\n\n**Risk Score: 72/100** - This frontend has significant security gaps that require immediate remediation before production deployment.\n\nThe most impactful fixes would be implementing httpOnly cookies for auth, enforcing HTTPS, adding CSRF protection, and enhancing error message handling.\n",
